WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:01.892
- Ezra enjoys gardening.

00:02.107 --> 00:04.661
Every sunflower plant he waters

00:04.661 --> 00:08.469
requires 0.7 liters of water,

00:08.469 --> 00:10.793
and every lily plant he waters

00:10.793 --> 00:13.510
requires 0.5 liters of water.

00:13.727 --> 00:18.022
Ezra has a total of 11 liters
of water for these plants.

00:18.313 --> 00:19.857
In the following inequality,

00:19.857 --> 00:22.270
S represents the number
of sunflower plants

00:22.270 --> 00:24.451
and L represents the number

00:24.451 --> 00:26.818
of lily plants Ezra can water.

00:27.098 --> 00:28.245
See if this makes sense.

00:28.308 --> 00:29.800
So it looks like...

00:29.852 --> 00:32.378
So the number of sunflower plants is S

00:32.627 --> 00:36.603
and he would have to use
7/10 of a liter per plant.

00:36.992 --> 00:39.076
So this first term right over here,

00:39.372 --> 00:40.795
this is how much water used

00:40.795 --> 00:43.318
to water the sunflower plants

00:43.508 --> 00:45.492
and then the second term is how much water

00:45.492 --> 00:47.544
used to water the lily plants

00:47.544 --> 00:51.184
cause he needs half a liter
for each of the L lily plants.

00:51.387 --> 00:53.355
And he has a total of 11 liters.

00:53.453 --> 00:54.928
So the sum right over here

00:54.928 --> 00:56.675
has to be less than or equal to 11.

00:56.994 --> 00:57.639
Alright.

00:57.783 --> 01:00.495
Ezra waters 10 lily plants.

01:00.686 --> 01:02.561
So that's L is equal to 10.

01:02.903 --> 01:05.991
How many sunflower plants
can he water at most

01:05.991 --> 01:08.342
with the remaining amount of water?

01:08.626 --> 01:10.060
Well let's think about this a little bit.

01:10.333 --> 01:12.243
We have 0.7,

01:13.026 --> 01:16.573
0.7 times the number of
sunflower plants he waters.

01:17.043 --> 01:19.255
Plus, plus...

01:19.655 --> 01:21.491
So we're gonna assume L is equal to 10.

01:21.491 --> 01:22.963
He waters 10 lily plants

01:22.963 --> 01:26.000
and each of them, he
gives half a liter to.

01:26.307 --> 01:27.602
So 0.5,

01:28.501 --> 01:32.373
0.5 x 10 is going to be 5.

01:32.808 --> 01:36.407
So it's gonna be five liters,
watering the 10 lily plants

01:36.407 --> 01:38.897
and this has to be less
than or equal to 11.

01:40.110 --> 01:44.179
So we can try to isolate
the S on the left hand side.

01:44.243 --> 01:46.530
So let's, let's do that.
The number of sunflowers.

01:46.530 --> 01:48.509
So we could first subtract
five from both sides.

01:49.327 --> 01:51.458
Subtract five from both sides.

01:51.707 --> 01:53.617
and we are going to be left with...

01:54.168 --> 01:56.920
We are going to be left
with on the left hand side,

01:57.800 --> 02:01.558
we're gonna just have 0.7 x S

02:02.028 --> 02:04.001
So this expression is
the total amount of water

02:04.001 --> 02:05.772
he's gonna spend on the sunflower plants

02:06.044 --> 02:08.286
has to be less than or equal to

02:08.286 --> 02:10.716
11- 5 is equal to six.

02:11.456 --> 02:14.931
And so now, we can
divide both sides by 0.7

02:15.784 --> 02:17.677
And we're gonna have to
change the inequality

02:17.677 --> 02:21.073
because we are diving by
a positive number, 0.7

02:21.484 --> 02:23.093
So we're gonna get S...

02:24.038 --> 02:26.777
S is less than or equal to

02:26.777 --> 02:29.588
6 ÷ 0.7

02:30.038 --> 02:31.648
or we could even write this as...

02:31.805 --> 02:33.808
we could write this as, well...

02:33.825 --> 02:37.395
This is 6 divided by 0.7

02:37.424 --> 02:38.730
Let me write everything as a fraction.

02:38.898 --> 02:43.455
This is the same thing as 6 ÷ 7/10

02:43.576 --> 02:48.576
which is equal to six times 10 over seven

02:48.974 --> 02:52.510
which is equal to 60/7

02:52.620 --> 02:55.168
which is equal to what is this?

02:55.174 --> 02:57.711
8 4/7

02:57.902 --> 03:02.273
so S has to be less than
eight and four sevenths.

03:02.476 --> 03:03.683
Now assuming that he's only,

03:03.683 --> 03:06.208
we're only thinking in
terms of whole plants...

03:06.214 --> 03:07.009
(mumbles)

03:07.049 --> 03:09.947
integer numbers but actually
whole numbers of plants

03:10.080 --> 03:13.319
and so, if S has to be less than 8 4/7,

03:13.319 --> 03:15.426
how many sunflower plants can he water

03:15.431 --> 03:17.307
at most with the
remaining amount of water?

03:17.602 --> 03:18.861
Well, we'll say that he had,

03:18.861 --> 03:20.593
most he can water eight plants.

03:20.833 --> 03:22.572
We're gonna assume that he can't water

03:22.572 --> 03:24.057
just a fraction of a plant.

03:24.057 --> 03:25.746
He either waters something or he doesn't.

03:25.972 --> 03:27.627
So he's gonna water eight,

03:27.795 --> 03:30.088
he is gonna water eight plants.

03:30.999 --> 03:32.961
Cause that's the largest whole number

03:32.961 --> 03:35.631
that is less than 8 4/7.

03:35.631 --> 03:36.316
That satisfies...

03:36.316 --> 03:39.480
That is less than or equal
to 8 4/7 I should say.
